<title>BULGARIA: Hewlett-Packard in Bulgarian telecom deal.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard in Bulgarian telecom deal.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Austrian branch of Hewlett-Packard Corp has signed a $5.7 million contract with the Bulgarian Telecommunication Company (BTC) for a management information system project, officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Hewlett-Packard will supply hardware and software for providing BTC with infrastructure for a modern data and management information system. The contract, signed on Monday, follows a tender on February 1.</p>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp France won a tender for a financial management system, which will cost $823,000. The BTC will negotiate with the firm and expects to sign a contract soon, BTC officials said.</p>
<p>-- Liliana Semerdjieva, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
